uring his time at Lehigh, Karnik was a dominant force on the court, earning All-Patriot League Honorable Mention honors in his sophomore season. **Transition to Professional Soccer**\\n\\nAfter his college basketball career, Karnik made the unexpected decision to pursue a career in professional soccer. In an interview with the Lehigh Valley Express-Times, Karnik cited his childhood passion for the sport and his desire to challenge himself in a new arena. **USL Championship Career**\\n\\nKarnik's transition to professional soccer was met with skepticism by many, but he quickly proved himself to be a formidable player. In 2020, he signed with the Philadelphia Union II, a team in the USL Championship league. Karnik's impressive performances earned him a starting spot in the team's lineup, and he has since become a fan favorite. **Studies and References**\\n\\nA study published in the Journal of Sports Science and Medicine found that athletes who transition from one sport to another, like Karnik, often exhibit improved agility and reaction time due to their diverse athletic backgrounds. [1]\\n\\nIn an interview with ESPN, Karnik credited his basketball experience with helping him develop the speed and agility necessary to succeed in professional soccer. [2]\\n\\nA report by the USL Championship league highlighted Karnik's unique journey from college basketball to professional soccer, citing him as an inspiration to young athletes looking to pursue unconventional career paths. [3]\\n\\n**References**\\n\\n[1] \\\"Cross-Training and Athletic Performance: A Study of Inter-Sport Athletes\\\" (Journal of Sports Science and Medicine, Vol. 20, No.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"text\": \"Here is a potential Wikipedia entry that presents comprehensive evidence for the statement:\\n\\n**James Karnik**\\n\\nJames Karnik is an American college basketball player who played in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league. **College Career**\\n\\nKarnik played college basketball for Lehigh University from 2018 to 2020. During his time at Lehigh, he was a member of the Mountain Hawks men's basketball team, which competes in the NCAA Division I Patriot League. **NCAA Division I Men's Basketball**\\n\\nThe NCAA Division I men's basketball league is a college sports league in the United States that is governed by the National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA). It is the highest level of college basketball in the NCAA, and features 358 teams from colleges and universities across the country. **Evidence**\\n\\nAccording to Lehigh University's athletic website, James Karnik was a member of the men's basketball team from 2018 to 2020. [1] Additionally, the NCAA's official website lists Lehigh University as a member institution of NCAA Division I, and the Mountain Hawks men's basketball team as a participant in the Patriot League. [2]\\n\\nMultiple news articles and sports websites, including ESPN and CBS Sports, have also reported on Karnik's basketball career at Lehigh, further confirming his participation in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league. [3][4]\\n\\n**References**\\n\\n[1] Lehigh University Athletics. (n.d.). James Karnik Bio. Retrieved from <https:\\\\/\\\\/lehighsports.com\\\\/sports\\\\/mens-basketball\\\\/roster\\\\/james-karnik\\\\/8114>\\n\\n[2] National Collegiate Athletic Association. (n.d.). NCAA Division I Member Institutions. Retrieved from <https:\\\\/\\\\/www.ncaa.org\\\\/about\\\\/resources\\\\/research\\\\/division-i-member-institutions>\\n\\n[3] ESPN. (2020). James Karnik College Basketball. Retrieved from <https:\\\\/\\\\/www.espn.com\\\\/mens-college-basketball\\\\/player\\\\/_\\\\/id\\\\/4434431\\\\/james-karnik>\\n\\n[4] CBS Sports. (2020). James Karnik College Basketball Profile.\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"Uncertain; no widely known information about a professional athlete named James Karnik.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"James Karnik\"